{"id": "R2791", "verdict": "platform-gap", "file": "catalog/agent-docs/model/jcl-operation-scripts.md", "heading": "Validation", "proposed": "A return statement in a script operation binding is checked against the bound operation: the output cardinality and output type must match. A mismatch is reported as \"don't match the output cardinality of operation '<Operation>'\" or \"... output type of operation '<Operation>'\". If the operation or one of its types cannot be resolved, the check passes without an error, so after you rename or retype an operation, run a full build and check the return statements of every script that calls it by hand.", "evidence": "models__judo-meta-script@5eb959b model/src/main/java/hu/blackbelt/judo/meta/script/validation/rules/OperationBindingValidations.java:304-306 (catch returns pass); binding.evl lines 4-20 (EVL messages)", "note": "Catalog has no text on operation-binding return checks. Evidence re-checked on the local judo-ng checkout (5eb959b), not on latest develop; line numbers may differ."}
{"id": "R2792", "verdict": "platform-gap", "file": "catalog/agent-docs/model/jcl-operation-scripts.md", "heading": "Validation", "proposed": "If the bound operation of a script operation binding cannot be found, the output-cardinality rule is skipped and reports nothing. After renaming an operation, check that every script binding still names an existing operation.", "evidence": "models__judo-meta-script@5eb959b model/src/main/java/hu/blackbelt/judo/meta/script/validation/rules/OperationBindingValidations.java:69-85 (guards return false when operation not found)", "note": "Not sure whether a separate rule reports a missing operation elsewhere; verify before publishing. Checked on 5eb959b, not latest develop."}
